To open a chest you can either:
1. <a>pply the chest while carrying it
2. #loot the chest while standing in the same square as the chest

To unlock a chest, you must <a>pply an unlocking tool while standing
in the same square as the chest, and either select [.] (here) or [>]
(down) as the direction to apply.  You cannot unlock a chest from an
adjacent square.  You can lock a chest in the same way.

Alternatively, you can break the lock on a chest with #force,
again in the [.] or [>] directions.  To do this you must be wielding a
weapon.  Be warned: edged weapons may break rather than breaking the
lock (yes, you can lose artifacts this way), and blunt weapons may
break the chest and some of its contents.  It's generally recommended
to use a disposable edged weapon such as an orcish dagger for this
purpose.

There are also some magics which will allow you to unlock (or lock)
chests.


